Let $k$ be the Mat'ern kernel with smoothness $
u > 0$. For a given $\delta \in (0,1)$, if REDS algorithm is run with $N_1 \geq C_{L_f, L_f'}\overline{N}(\delta/\log_2(T))$ under noise-free feedback on a function $f \in \cH_k$ satisfying Assumption~ef{assumption:f_level_set_regularity}, then the regret incurred by REDS satisfies,  
     egin{align*}
        R(T) =  egin{cases} 	ilde{\cO}(T^{1 - 
u/d}) & 	ext{ if } 
u < d, \ \cO((\log T)^{5/2}) & 	ext{ if } 
u = d, \ \cO((\log T)^{3/2}) & 	ext{ if } 
u > d.\end{cases}.
    \end{align*}
    with probability at least $1 - \delta$.
